<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alceste De Ambris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alceste De Ambris was an Italian revolutionary syndicalist and trade union organiser. He campaigned for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and in 1920 drafted with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriele-dannunzio">Gabriele D'Annunzio</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charter-of-carnaro">Charter of Carnaro</a>, the constitution of the regency at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Fiume</a>. He later opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a> and died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alceste-de-ambris.jpg" alt="Alceste De Ambris" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alceste_de_Ambris_1930.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
